    ThreadedHasher.cpp, CheevosIndex.cpp: the lookup-only startup pass runs once a day at most (audit #186 PL-08, the cost)
    
    A lookup pass with nothing to hash beside it still fetches the hash
    library -- two requests, several megabytes, on the interface thread at
    startup -- and nearly every library holds a game RetroAchievements does not
    know (a hack, a bad dump) whose hash and empty id would ask for it at every
    boot, where before an indexed library asked for nothing. So the silent
    startup run makes the pass at most once a day, by a stamp in es_settings.cfg
    (CheevosLookupOnlyLast) written once the library has come, so an offline
    boot does not spend the day's pass on a fetch that failed. A run the player
    asked for, or one with games to hash, is not held back. The rule is
    CheevosIndex::lookupDue, with a unit test: due when none has run, when a
    day has passed, or when the clock went back.
    
